#: angular/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A standalone Angular app (via Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, no "
"Angular CLI) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"and\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken custom elements\n"
"for Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` calls `registerPantokenElements()` (from `@pantoken/"
"angular`) once at bootstrap so\n"
"  elements like `<instui-icon>` work in templates, and imports the token/"
"component CSS plus\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, and other component "
"behaviors out of the\n"
"  box).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` is a standalone component (`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` "
"lets the template\n"
"  compiler accept pantoken's custom element tags) whose template is styled "
"with `instui-*`\n"
"  classes; optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"are marked with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"He taupānga Angular tū-tahi (maehe Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, "
"kāore he Angular CLI) i whakakakahu ki\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"me\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) (ngā "
"āhua ritenga pantoken\n"
"mō Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Whakawhanake\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## He aha kei konei\n"
"\n"
"- Ka karanga a `src/main.ts` i a `registerPantokenElements()` (nā `@pantoken/"
"angular`) kotahi i te tīmatanga kia\n"
"  mahi ai ngā āhuatanga pēnei i `<instui-icon>` i roto i ngā tauira, ā, ka "
"kawemai hoki i te CSS token/komihana me\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (ka hono i te modal, tooltip, me ētahi atu "
"whanonga kōtaha, kua rite mai).\n"
"- He kōtaha tū-tahi a `src/app.component.ts` (`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` e "
"tuku ana ki te kaiwhakawa tauira kia\n"
"  whakaae ki ngā tūāhua ritenga a pantoken) e whakakakahu ana tana tauira ki "
"ngā karaehe `instui-*`;\n"
"  ko ngā wāhi whakauru kōwhiringa (taitara, tātari, ihirangi, ā muri) kua "
"tohu ki te `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Whakamahia ngā karaehe pērā i `class=\"instui-button\"` ki ngā tohu; "
"tirohia te\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) mō te rārangi karaehe "
"katoa.\n"
"\n"
"## Akohia atu\n"
"\n"
"Tirohia te [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-"
"started) kia ako ake.\n"

#: canvas-theme-editor/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Upload-ready assets for Canvas LMS's **Theme Editor**, plus a local preview "
"for authoring Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) page templates styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — upload these two files under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** in Canvas.\n"
"  They're built for the CDN provider/theme/mode you chose when scaffolding "
"(`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light by default) and include a loader "
"for\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up component behaviors like modal, "
"tooltip, and drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — a local, TinyMCE-based editor (`npm run "
"dev`) that mirrors Canvas's\n"
"  RCE so you can author page templates against pantoken's classes before "
"copying them into Canvas.\n"
"  The page itself is built with pantoken's `wrapper` layout: click **Edit "
"theme** to open a tray\n"
"  with **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** tabs (CDN provider/theme/mode selects, "
"and syntax-highlighted,\n"
"  hand-editable copies of `theme.css`/`theme.js` that feed the live "
"preview), and the **?** button\n"
"  for full instructions. Use the **Layouts** toolbar button to start from "
"one of pantoken's bundled\n"
"  starter page layouts (hero, callout, two-column, rubric note, "
"testimonial), sourced from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"This opens a Vite dev server with:\n"
"\n"
"- An **editor** pane (TinyMCE, matching the version/config\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) itself "
"uses — see below).\n"
"  Use the **Layouts** button to load one of the bundled starter layouts "
"(this replaces the whole\n"
"  document, after a confirm, rather than inserting at the cursor), and the "
"**Source code** toggle\n"
"  to hand-edit the raw HTML in a syntax-highlighted (CodeMirror) view "
"alongside the editor, with\n"
"  the preview pane updating live as you type — unlike TinyMCE's stock `code` "
"plugin, which edits in\n"
"  a one-shot modal dialog with no live preview.\n"
"- A **preview** pane showing the editor's content with the current CSS/JS "
"tab's stylesheet/script\n"
"  applied (not just the resolved CDN URLs), wrapped to match Canvas's own "
"content-area background\n"
"  and max width — a faithful \"what this will look like once uploaded to "
"Canvas\" check, updated\n"
"  live as you type or edit the theme.\n"
"- The editor and preview panes sit in a split view you can resize by "
"dragging the divider, stack\n"
"  vertically instead of side by side, and swap the order of (drag a pane's "
"toolbar onto the other,\n"
"  or use the **Swap panes** button). Each pane has its own fullscreen "
"button.\n"
"- The **Edit theme** tray's **Config** tab holds the CDN provider/theme/mode "
"selects and\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js** links; its **CSS**/**JS** "
"tabs are editable copies\n"
"  of the generated files — hand-edit them and the preview picks up your "
"changes directly. Changing\n"
"  a Config select re-generates the CSS/JS tabs unless you've already edited "
"them, in which case a\n"
"  **Regenerate from config** button appears instead of silently overwriting "
"your edit.\n"
"\n"
"## Workflow\n"
"\n"
"1. Upload `theme.css` and `theme.js` to Canvas's Theme Editor (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) so\n"
"   pantoken's classes are available on every page.\n"
"2. Run `npm run dev`, use **Layouts** to start from a bundled starter, and "
"edit it like you\n"
"   would in Canvas's own RCE.\n"
"3. Click **Copy HTML** and paste the result into a Canvas page's RCE (switch "
"to the HTML editor\n"
"   view first). Canvas sanitizes pasted HTML server-side — this scaffold "
"doesn't attempt to\n"
"   replicate that, so always verify the pasted result in Canvas (see \"Notes "
"on Canvas's RCE\"\n"
"   below).\n"
"\n"
"## Notes on Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"The Canvas Rich Content Editor runs TinyMCE and sanitizes submitted HTML on "
"the server against an\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` in canvas-lms, kept in sync with TinyMCE's "
"own\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). What that allowlist means for "
"templates built here:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, and `aria-*` attributes are "
"allowed on every element —\n"
"  pantoken's `class=\"instui-*\"` styling hooks (and inline `style`, e.g. "
"for CSS anchor positioning)\n"
"  **do** survive being pasted and saved, contrary to older guidance in this "
"file. `<script>` tags\n"
"  are always stripped.\n"
"- **RCE-safe pantoken components**: static/display components — alert, view, "
"heading, text, table,\n"
"  a button-as-`<a>` (not a real `<button>`), blockquote. Stick to semantic "
"HTML pantoken already\n"
"  supports (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- **RCE-unsafe**: anything from `@pantoken/interactions`'s behavior set — "
"modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, or any other component driven by the native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributes. Those attributes aren't in Canvas's "
"sanitizer allowlist, so\n"
"  the markup survives but the interactive behavior silently breaks the first "
"time the page is\n"
"  saved in Canvas, even with `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader "
"present. Real form\n"
"  elements (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) and "
"inline `<svg>` are\n"
"  stripped outright — none of the bundled starter templates use them.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` loads `@pantoken/interactions` from the CDN, which runs in "
"Canvas's global page scope —\n"
"useful for interactions on pages you build directly in Canvas's RCE with raw "
"HTML edits, but (per\n"
"above) any `popover`/`command`-attribute-driven markup pasted from the RCE "
"preview here won't stay\n"
"interactive once saved.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Ngā rawa kua rite kia tuku mō te Kaiwhakatika Kaupapa (Theme Editor) o "
"Canvas LMS, me tētahi arotakenga ā-rohe mō te tuhi tauira whārangi Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) kua āhua-iho ki te\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## He aha kei konei\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — tuku ēnei kōnae e rua i raro i **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** i Canvas.\n"
"  I hanga ēnei mō te kaiwhakarato CDN/kaupapa/āhua i tīpakohia e koe i te wā "
"o te scaffolding (`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light mō te taunoa) ā, kei roto hoki he "
"kaikawe mō\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (e hono ana i ngā whanonga wāhanga pērā i te "
"modal, tooltip, me te drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — he editor ā-rohe, ā-tinyMCE (`npm run dev`) "
"e kapi ana i te RCE o Canvas kia taea e koe te tuhituhi tauira whārangi ki "
"ngā kara o pantoken i mua i te tārua ki Canvas.\n"
"  I hanga te whārangi mā te rārangi `wrapper` a pantoken: pāwhiritia te "
"**Edit theme** kia whakatuwheratia tētahi pae\n"
"  me ngā ripa **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** (ngā kōwhiringa kaiwhakarato CDN/"
"kaupapa/āhua, me ngā tārua he wāhanga-kōrero-āwhiti,\n"
"  ka taea te whakatika ā-ringa o `theme.css`/`theme.js` e whakarato ana i te "
"arotakenga ora), me te pātene **?**\n"
"  mō ngā tohutohu katoa. Whakamahia te pātene taputapu **Layouts** kia "
"tīmata i tētahi o ngā aratau whārangi tīmata o pantoken (hero, callout, two-"
"column, rubric note, testimonial), i tangohia mai i\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Whanake\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Ka whakatuwhera tēnei i tētahi tūmau whakawhanake Vite me:\n"
"\n"
"- He anga **editor** (TinyMCE, e rite ana ki te putanga/config\n"
"  e whakamahia ana e [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/"
"canvas-lms) — titiro iho). Whakamahia te pātene **Layouts** kia utaina "
"tētahi o ngā aratau tīmata kua tāpirihia (ka whakakapi i te tuhinga katoa, i "
"muri i te whakaaetanga, kaua ki te tāpiri ki te tohu), me te whakawhiti "
"**Source code**\n"
"  kia whakatika ā-ringa i te HTML matawai i roto i tētahi tirohanga kua "
"whakanikonikotia te wetereo (CodeMirror) kei te taha o te editor, ā, ka "
"whakahou tonu te arotakenga i te wā e tuhituhi ana koe — ehara i te āhua o "
"te pūtene `code` o TinyMCE, e whakatika ana i roto i tētahi pouaka modal "
"kotahi-wa me te kore arotakenga ora.\n"
"- He anga **preview** e whakaatu ana i ngā ihirangi o te editor me te "
"raupapa kuputuhi/waehere o tēnei ripa CSS/JS kua tonoa (ehara i te "
"utuputanga URL CDN anake), kua takai kia rite ki te papamuri me te whānui "
"mōrahi o te rohe ihirangi o Canvas — he whakamātautau pono “tēnei te āhua i "
"te wā kua tukuna ki Canvas” e whakahou ana ora i te wā e tuhituhi ana kia "
"whakatikahia te kaupapa.\n"
"- Kei ngā anga editor me preview i roto i tētahi tirohanga wāwāhi ka taea te "
"whakarahi mā te toia te wāwehenga, ka whakakaha poutū hei utu mō te taha ki "
"te taha, ā, ka taea te whakawhiti i te raupapa o ngā anga (toia te pae "
"taputapu o tētahi anga ki runga i tētahi atu, kāore rānei whakamahi i te "
"pātene **Swap panes**). Ia anga he pātene mata-katoa tōna.\n"
"- Kei te pae **Edit theme** ripa **Config** ngā kōwhiringa kaiwhakarato CDN/"
"kaupapa/āhua me ngā hononga **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js**; "
"ko āna ripa **CSS**/**JS** he tārua ka whakatuhia o ngā kōnae — whakatikahia "
"ā-ringa ā-rānei ka kitea e te arotakenga ngā panoni tonu. Mēnā ka "
"whakarerekē koe i tētahi kōwhiringa Config ka hanga anō i ngā ripa CSS/JS, "
"kia kore rānei kua whakatikahia e koe ēnei i mua, ā, ka puta tētahi pātene "
"**Regenerate from config** hei utu i te whakakapi huna i tō whakatika.\n"
"\n"
"## Tukanga mahi\n"
"\n"
"1. Tuku `theme.css` me `theme.js` ki te Theme Editor o Canvas (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) kia wātea ngā kara o pantoken i ia whārangi.\n"
"2. Whakahaere `npm run dev`, whakamahi **Layouts** kia tīmata i tētahi "
"tīmata kua tāpirihia, ā, whakatikahia pērā i tō mahi ki te RCE o Canvas.\n"
"3. Pāwhiritia **Copy HTML** ka whakapiri i te hua ki te RCE o tētahi "
"whārangi Canvas (whakawhiti ki te tirohanga etita HTML i mua). Ka "
"whakamaoritia e Canvas te HTML kua whakapirihia ki te tūmau — kāore tēnei "
"scaffolding e tātaritia taua tukanga, nō reira me tirohia tonu te hua kua "
"whakapirihia i roto i Canvas (titiro ki te \"Ngā whakamārama mō te RCE o "
"Canvas\" i raro).\n"
"\n"
"## Ngā whakamārama mō te RCE o Canvas\n"
"\n"
"Kei te whakahaere TinyMCE te Canvas Rich Content Editor ā, ka whakahaua te "
"HTML kua tukuna ki te tūmau kia whakataetia ki tētahi rārangi āhei "
"(allowlist) (`gems/canvas_sanitize` i canvas-lms, kia ū tonu ki ngā "
"āhuatanga o TinyMCE\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). Ēnei mea e tohu ana mō ngā "
"tauira kua waihangatia i konei:\n"
"\n"
"- He rāpoi āhei ngā āhuatanga `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, me "
"`aria-*` ki runga i ia āhuatanga —\n"
"  ka **ora** tonu ngā tūāpapa whakapaipai o pantoken (`class=\"instui-*\"`) "
"(me ngā `style` ā-ringa, hei tauira mō te whakatakoto tātai CSS)\n"
"  contrary ki ngā tohutohu tawhito i roto i tēnei kōnae. Ka tango tonu ngā "
"tapanga `<script>`.\n"
"- Ngā **wāhanga pantoken haumaru mō te RCE**: ngā wāhanga tūmau/arā whakaatu "
"— alert, view, heading, text, table,\n"
"  he pātene-as-`<a>` (ehara i te `<button>` tūturu), blockquote. Aro atu ki "
"te HTML ā-tikanga e tautokohia e pantoken (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, "
"headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- **Kāore i te haumaru ki te RCE**: he aha rānei i te rōpū whanonga o "
"`@pantoken/interactions` — modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, me ērā atu wāhanga e whakaohoa ana e ngā "
"āhuatanga ā-hāngai o te pūnaha `popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor`. Kāore ēnei āhuatanga i roto i te rārangi āhei o te "
"kaimātai Canvas, nō reira\n"
"  ka noho te tohu engari ka pakaru te whanonga tāpiri i te wā tuatahi ka "
"whakaora te whārangi i Canvas, ahakoa te aitua o te kaikawe `theme.js` "
"`@pantoken/interactions`. Ka tangohia ngā āhuatanga o ngā puka tūturu "
"(`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) me ngā `<svg>` ā-"
"ringa — kāore rānei i whakamahia i ngā tauira tīmata kua tāpirihia.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` e utaina ana `@pantoken/interactions` mai i te CDN, e whakahaere "
"ana i te rohe whārangi ao o Canvas —\n"
"he whaihua mō ngā whakawhitinga i runga i ngā whārangi ka waihangatia e koe "
"tika i roto i te RCE o Canvas me ngā whakatikanga HTML matau, engari (pērā i "
"runga ake nei) kāore ngā tohu āhuatanga-`popover`/`command`-e ārahi ana kua "
"whakapirihia mai i te arotakenga o konei e noho tonu\n"
"hei rawa mahi i te wā ka whakaora.\n"

#: components/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A plain TypeScript app (via Vite) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructure's\n"
"design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` holds the actual page markup — a `wrapper`-layout shell from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). View source\n"
"  and edit it directly; nothing is injected by JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` imports `@pantoken/css` (defines every `--instui-*` custom "
"property),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (document defaults + focus ring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` classes), `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, "
"and other component\n"
"  behaviors out of the box), and your own `src/style.css` — add interactive "
"behavior here.\n"
"- Optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) are marked "
"with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` in `index.html` — replace their contents with "
"your own markup.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [HTML guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"He taupānga TypeScript māmā (ma te Vite) i whakaritea ki te āhua mā\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), ngā tohu hoahoa me ngā tohu ā-ata o Instructure.\n"
"\n"
"## Whakawhanake\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## He aha kei konei\n"
"\n"
"- Ko `index.html` te pupuri i te tohu whārangi tūturu — he anga-`wrapper` "
"nō\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). Tirohia te putanga puna\n"
"  ka whakatika tika; kāore he mea whakauruia e JavaScript.\n"
"- Ka kawemai e `src/main.ts` a `@pantoken/css` (e tautuhia ana ngā `--instui-"
"*` rawa ritenga katoa),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (ngā taunoa tuhinga + te rīngi arotahi), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (ngā karaehe `.instui-*`), `@pantoken/interactions` (e hono ana i te "
"aronga modal, tooltip, me\n"
"  ērā atu whanonga wāhanga mai i te tīmatatanga), me tō ake `src/style.css` "
"— tāpirihia ngā\n"
"  whanonga whakauru ki konei.\n"
"- Ko ngā waahi tāpiri ā-kōwhiringa (tūhono matua, tātari, ihirangi, "
"whakakapi) e tohu ana ki te\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` i roto i `index.html` — whakakapia ō rātou "
"ihirangi ki tō ake tohu.\n"
"- Tāpirihia ngā karaehe pērā i `class=\"instui-button\"` ki ngā tohu; "
"tirohia te\n"
"  [tohu wāhanga](https://pantoken.app/api/css) mō te rārangi karaehe katoa.\n"
"\n"
"## Ako atu\n"
"\n"
"Tirohia te [aratohu HTML](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) kia ako "
"ake.\n"

#: next/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A Next.js (App Router) app styled with [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructure's design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` wraps the config with `withPantoken(...)` (adds pantoken "
"to\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` imports `@pantoken/css`, which defines every `--instui-*` "
"custom\n"
"  property, at the root so it's available on every page, plus the `wrapper` "
"layout's root class on\n"
"  `<body>` and `PantokenInteractions` (a client component that loads "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  wires up modal, tooltip, and other component behaviors out of the box).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` renders markup styled with `instui-*` classes; optional "
"insertion points (header,\n"
"  filters, content, trailing) are marked with `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"He taupānga Next.js (App Router) kua whakapaipaihia mā te [`@pantoken/next`]"
"(https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next), ngā tohu hoahoa me ngā tohu "
"whakaahua a Instructure.\n"
"\n"
"## Whakawhanake\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## He aha kei konei\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` ka whakamau i te whirihora ki `withPantoken(...)` (ka "
"tāpiri i te pantoken ki `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` ka kawemai i a `@pantoken/css`, e tautuhi ana i ia `--"
"instui-*` rawa māna, kei te pakiaka kia wātea ai ki ia whārangi, ā, tae atu "
"ki te kara matua o te whakatakotoranga `wrapper` kei runga i `<body>` me "
"`PantokenInteractions` (he wāhanga kiritaki e uta ana i `@pantoken/"
"interactions` — ka hono ngā aratau pātaka, taputapu tohu, me ētahi atu "
"whanonga waahanga i te tīmata).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` ka whakaputa tohu hākoritanga kua āta hoahoahia ki ngā kara "
"`instui-*`; ko ngā wāhi whakauruhia kōwhiringa (upoko, tātari, ihirangi, "
"mutunga) kua tohua ki `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"\n"
"## Ako atu\n"
"\n"
"Tirohia te [aratohu tīmata](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) kia "
"mōhio atu.\n"

#: react/README.md
